-- ============================================================================
-- DR11 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Well Integrity & P&A, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions. The structure row is GENERATED from
-- the tier's manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: the annulus pressure limits that protect the barriers
-- the Associate tier learned to read. A row per bounding element, the RP 90
-- design factors, and the case where the annulus cannot be pressured at all.
--
-- EVERY NUMBER IN THIS TIER IS A DIFFERENCE, NOT A LEVEL. A rating is a
-- difference across a wall, an allowable is a rating less a head, and a
-- governing value is the smallest of those differences. A reader who asks
-- "difference between what and what" gets every question in the tier right.
--
-- THE INVERSION: THE ROLE, NOT THE PIPE, SETS THE LIMIT. The same steel at the
-- same depth allows very different pressures depending on which role it plays,
-- because an outer casing is harder to inspect, harder to repair and its
-- failure is harder to detect, so it is trusted less. On the published fixture
-- the spread across the five roles is 20 MPa on ONE piece of pipe, which is
-- slightly more than double the allowable at the strictest role. So the
-- element with the HIGHEST rating can govern the annulus, and often does.
--
-- THE FAR SIDE IS PART OF THE ANSWER. A heavier column on the far side pushes
-- back and RAISES the allowable here; a heavier column on this side lowers it.
-- The sensitivity is g times the true vertical depth, independent of the
-- rating and the factor. Leaving the backup density blank means assuming GAS,
-- which is the conservative reading and also the one that most often drives a
-- row negative. There is no free margin, only a choice about where to spend it.
--
-- AND THE GOVERNING ROW IS A REDUCTION, NOT A ROW. It is the MINIMUM over the
-- rows and it is not the first one. Verifying every row does not verify the
-- fold over them, which is a mistake a sibling course shipped in a different
-- engine and paid for. The clamp to zero and the negative flag are applied
-- AFTER the pick and describe the governing row only.
--
-- WHEN THE ANSWER IS NEGATIVE IT IS A FINDING, NOT A PRESSURE. Hydrostatic
-- alone can exceed a rating. The engine reports the maximum of zero and the
-- governing row and raises a flag, because reporting a negative allowable as
-- though it were a pressure you could apply would be worse than useless.
-- ============================================================================

values ('integrity', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-why-annulus-pressure-matters","title":"Why Annulus Pressure Matters","lesson_keys":["l01-a-sealed-volume-that-heats-up","l02-what-a-limit-protects","l03-maasp-and-mawop-are-different","l04-what-this-tier-computes"]},{"key":"m02-maasp","title":"MAASP","lesson_keys":["l01-a-row-for-every-element","l02-the-rating-term","l03-the-hydrostatic-term","l04-the-governing-row","l05-reading-the-table"]},{"key":"m03-mawop-and-the-rp90-factors","title":"MAWOP and the RP 90 Factors","lesson_keys":["l01-a-design-factor-by-role","l02-why-an-outer-string-is-derated","l03-the-governing-candidate","l04-the-inversion","l05-wear-derating"]},{"key":"m04-the-differential","title":"The Differential","lesson_keys":["l01-a-rating-is-across-a-wall","l02-what-is-on-the-far-side","l03-the-fluid-that-pushes-back","l04-a-heavier-annulus-buys-margin","l05-and-takes-it-away-elsewhere"]},{"key":"m05-when-it-cannot-be-pressured","title":"When It Cannot Be Pressured","lesson_keys":["l01-unloading-the-tubing-to-gas","l02-a-negative-row","l03-the-clamp-to-zero","l04-what-a-negative-maasp-obliges"]},{"key":"m06-the-professional-reading","title":"The Professional Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
